## DEFINITION
ExPASy ProtParam is an online tool that computes the physical and chemical properties of a protein from its amino acid sequence.

## PURPOSE
- Analyze protein physicochemical properties.
- Estimate protein stability and composition.
- Support protein characterization.
- Assist in protein research and bioinformatics studies.

## PARAMETERS CALCULATED
- Molecular weight
- Theoretical isoelectric point (pI)
- Amino acid composition
- Extinction coefficient
- Instability index
- Aliphatic index
- GRAVY (Grand Average of Hydropathicity)

## APPLICATIONS
- Protein characterization.
- Stability prediction.
- Comparative protein analysis.
- Recombinant protein research.

## FILES TO UPLOAD
- Protein FASTA (.fasta, .fa)
- Protein sequence (.txt)
- UniProt accession ID

## IMPORTANT POINTS
- Accepts protein sequences only.
- Calculates properties without requiring a 3D structure.
- Fast and freely accessible.
- Commonly used before protein structure and function analysis.
